d not contradictable — not a defect. But \"Quest\" generic vs \"主线任务\" specific — an added \"main\". Weak. I might report UNCERTAIN for ADDITION. Hmm. Many translation QA would flag. I'll report UNCERTAIN? Or skip. Let me consider: the string is generic \"Quest ... Failed!\" used for any quest, so labeling as main quest is wrong contextually but not verifiable from visible text. I'll report UNCERTAIN ADDITION with evidence \"Quest #CIMSON#Failed!\" and correction \"任务 #CIMSON#失败了！\". Actually, hmm. I'll include it as UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ007: \"You must wear this object to use it!\" → \"你必须装备这件物品才能使用它！\" \"wear\" → \"装备\" fine. OK.\n\nQ008: \"Click to copy to clipboard.\" → \"点击复制。\" (clipboard omitted, fine). \"You can share the wanderer seed with your friends, this way they can play with the same set of talents.\" → \"你可以将流浪者随机种子分享给朋友，这样你们可以用同一套技能组合进行游玩。\" \"they\" → \"你们\" — source says they (friends) can play with same talents; target says 你们 (you all) can play. Slight SUBJECT shift: source emphasizes friends can play same set; target \"你们\" includes you. Minor, arguably fine. \"wanderer seed\" → \"流浪者随机种子\" fine. I'll not report. Hmm, \"they\" vs \"你们\" — could be SUBJECT finding. It's minor; the meaning \"same set of talents\" preserved. Skip.\n\nQ009: \"Spare me the small talk. I am here to stop you!\" → \"我不是来和你们聊天的，我是来阻止你们的！\" Fine. \"Spare me\" → \"我不是来...聊天的\" — meaning preserved-ish. OK.\n\nQ010: \"Display mouse gesture trails\" → \"隐藏鼠标手势轨迹\" — Display → 隐藏. Clear DIRECTION/value flip. FINDING. Correction: \"显示鼠标手势轨迹\". Evidence \"Display mouse gesture trails\".\n\nQ011: \"I cannot, but I may show you a glimpse. ... This is the Way.\" → \"不行，不过我可以让你看一下。... 这不是维网。\" — \"This is the Way\" translated as \"这不是维网\" (\"This is NOT the Weave\"). Major negation error and \"维网\" (Weave) — hmm, \"the Way\" vs \"维网\"? Wait, \"维网\" could be translation of \"the Weave\" (D&D). Source says \"This is the Way.\" Target: \"这不是维网。\" Both negation added and referent changed. FINDING. claim_type: could be OTHER/ADDition of negation... Let me pick two candidates? One: negation added (\"不是\") — claim_type OTHER or ADDITION? Actually the defect: target negates. I'd use claim_type \"OTHER\" or \"STATE\"? Hmm. Categories: ADDITION (added \"不\"), REFERENT (\"the Way\" → \"维网\"). Report two candidates: (1) negation, (2) referent. Actually maybe simpler one candidate: \"This is the Way\" mistranslated as \"这不是维网\" — correction \"这就是道。\" or \"这就是'道'。\" Given context: \"This is the Way.\" Target \"这不是维网。\" I'll report one FINDING with claim_type OTHER? Better: two candidates — one for the negation (ADDITION of \"不\"), one for REFERENT (\"Way\"→\"维网\"). Evidence \"This is the Way.\" Both spans: \"这不是维网\" — but target_span must be verbatim in target; both candidates can use \"这不是维网。\" Hmm spans identical is allowed. I'll do two candidates.\n\nActually wait — is \"维网\" a mistranslation? In ToME, \"the Way\" might be a specific concept. Hmm, ToME's Celestial/Anorithil... \"This is the Way\" — could be from a psionic/mindslayer context? Actually \"I cannot, but I may show you a glimpse... feelings of peace and happiness... This is the Way.\" Might be the Sunwall path? Without external knowledge, \"the Way\" → \"维网\" is a referent change supported by the source itself (\"the Way\" vs \"维网\"). Since translation should render \"the Way\", rendering as \"维网\" changes the term. But could \"维网\" be the game's established translation of \"the Way\"? Unlikely — \"Weave\" fits 维网 better. From visible evidence alone: source term is \"the Way\", target term is \"维网\" — that's a lexical mismatch, objectively. And \"不是\" adds negation, clearly objective. I'll report the negation as FINDING (strong), and the referent as FINDING too or UNCERTAIN. I'll do negation FINDING and referent UNCERTAIN? Hmm, if \"维网\" were the canonical translation of \"the Way\", referent candidate wrong. I'll mark referent UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ012: \"Open profile(in browser)\" → \"打开我的用户信息（在浏览器里打开）